    "q-176863": {
      "dom_id": "step-q176863",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "$10$ is **not** a prime number, and $0.1$ is a real number.\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following:\n\n- $P:10\\text{ is a prime number}$\n\n- $Q:0.1\\text{ is a real number}$",
      "worked_solution": "The negation is represented by the symbol \"$¬$\".\n\nThe sentence\n\n$10$ is **not** a prime number \n\ncan be expressed symbolically as $¬P.$ \n\nThe sentence\n\n$0.1$ is a real number \n\ncan be expressed symbolically as $Q.$\n\nTherefore, the sentence\n\n$10$ is **not** a prime number, and $0.1$ is a real number\n\ncan be expressed symbolically as $¬P∧Q.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
