      "dom_id": "step-q176865",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "$\\frac{1}{2}$ is **not** a rational number, or $-2$ is negative.\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following:\n\n- $P:\\frac{1}{2}\\text{ is a rational number}$\n\n- $Q:-2\\text{ is negative}$",
      "worked_solution": "The sentence\n\n$\\frac{1}{2}$ is **not** a rational number \n\ncan be expressed symbolically as $¬P.$ \n\nThe sentence\n\n$-2$ is negative\n\ncan be expressed symbolically as $Q.$\n\nTherefore, the sentence\n\n$\\frac{1}{2}$ is **not** a rational number, or $-2$ is negative\n\ncan be expressed symbolically as $¬P∨Q.$",
