    "q-182392": {
      "dom_id": "step-q182392",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Find the missing values in the following truth table:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬(A∧B)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-4}} |",
      "worked_solution": "First, we add a column for $A∧B.$ Remember that $A∧B$ is true if both $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A∧B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nThen, we add a column for $¬(A∧B).$ Remember that the truth values of $¬(A∧B)$ are opposite those of $A∧B.$\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A∧B\\,$ | $\\,¬(A∧B)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
