      "name": "Question 17",
      "problem": "Simplify the statement $¬[¬(¬B∨¬(¬A))].$",
      "worked_solution": "Two negations in a row cancel each other out. So, we can simplify  $¬(¬A)$ to $A.$ \n\nAs a result of this, the statement simplifes to \n\n$$\n¬[¬(¬B∨A)]\n$$\n\nThen, we can simplify $¬(¬(¬B∨A))$ to $¬B∨A.$\n\nTherefore, the given statement can be simplified to \n\n$$\n¬B∨A.\n$$",
