      "name": "Question 19",
      "problem": "Simplify the statement $¬[¬(A∧¬(¬B))]∨B.$",
      "worked_solution": "Two negations in a row cancel each other out. So, we can simplify $¬(¬B)$ to $B.$ \n\nAs a result of this, the statement simplifes to \n\n$$\n¬(¬(A∧B))∨B.\n$$\n\nThen, we can simplify $¬(¬(A∧B))$ to $A∧B.$\n\nTherefore, the given statement can be simplified to \n\n$$\n(A∧B)∨B.\n$$",
